"""EdgeLens NBA player points.

The EdgeLens NBA model: P(player finishes with at least `line` points | live state), from
gradient-boosted trees (scikit-learn HistGradientBoosting, 250 trees) trained on 2024-25 NBA
play-by-play on lines up to 50 points beyond the player's score (model v3, 2026-11-06) and
isotonic-calibrated on the first half of 2025-26. Same trees as the EdgeLens extension, evaluated
here in plain Python.

Inputs come from market["player_state"]: game time, points, minutes, fouls, on the floor, team
margin, and season points per minute and minutes per game. It sits out the first minute, overtime,
players with too little history, lines already reached, and lines more than 50 points away (beyond
what the model was trained on).

Trades the EdgeLens NBA paper strategy: 1 contract the first time Yes or No is at least 5 cents
better than fair after the taker fee, at most one Yes and one No per market, held to settlement.
Set FOURTH_QUARTER_ONLY to True to trade only in the 4th quarter.

Backtest with league NBA and market type "Player points". Live runs have no play-by-play feed,
so the model sits out.
"""
